# {name}

An OpenAI Agents SDK agent that remembers the people it talks to, with
[Alexein](https://alexein.ai). Made by `npx @alexein/cli create openai-agents`.

## Run it

1. Fill in `.env`: `ALEXEIN_API_KEY` (the console, under API keys) and `OPENAI_API_KEY`.
2. Talk to it in a terminal, as one of your users:

   ```bash
   npm run chat -- --user dana
   ```

3. `npx @alexein/cli doctor` checks the setup.

## What is where

- `src/agent.ts` - the agent: memory is wired in here.
- `src/memory.ts` - memory's settings and the `AlexeinMemory` the agent uses, written by
  `npx @alexein/cli init openai-agents`. Yours to edit; recall, remember and the tools themselves
  come from [`@alexein/sdk/openai-agents`](https://docs.alexein.ai/sdks/typescript).
- `src/chat.ts` - the terminal chat.

Whose memory a run reads is the `userId` in its context, set by your code and never by the model.
